{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id175424361"}, "name":{"label":"KenHoodCafe"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-11-16T19:52:51-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.22.4"}, "id":{"label":"13407580631"}, "title":{"label":"Really amazing."}, "content":{"label":"(From my 8 favorite apps review series on Facebook)\n\nThis award winning app is the only app I’ve ever taken the risk of buying without a free look. They are so boss, they can just charge straight up for it. $9.99 one-time.\n\nIt’s a to-do list that looks deceptively simple. I love the beautiful interface. So clean and simple. A total Apple-look. But tons of power and potential under the hood. I’m still finding more ways almost every day to organize my life with it.\n\nThink of it as a hybrid to-do list and a project organizer. Groceries, to multi step and multi day detailed projects. It is sweet at both ends.\n\nMy favorite among many “wow” features is how easy it is to “punt” a to-do that’s undone at the end of the day to: tomorrow, or a future date, or “someday.” \n\nYou can organize things into “Areas” and “Projects,” or just leave some to-do’s hang loose unassigned. Moving, shifting, and re categorizing is dumb-dumb simple.\n\nIt gets 5 Stars in my defeat-friction hall of fame.\n\nIf you are not totally in love with your list/to-do/project planner… risk the ten bucks on this. I promise, you won’t be disappointed.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=904237743&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
